= Probability distribution — Simple =

A '''probability distribution''' shows how probability is spread across possible values.

For a six-sided fair die, the values 1 through 6 each have probability 1/6.

That is a simple discrete distribution.

Continuous measurements, such as height or temperature, use distributions where probability is assigned to ranges of values.

A distribution is a mathematical model.

A histogram is a picture of observed data, so it is not exactly the same thing as a probability distribution.

